xt": "G4 lost 25.3 points, taking Black's lead from +13.1 to +38.5, with H5 the engine's choice. The 12k answered with H4, which lost 27.0 and dropped the lead to +11.4. Both sides handed the same big swing back and forth in this fight around G4, H4 and H3."}, {"turn": 27, "text": "The 12k's H6 was their worst move, 33.5 points lost, from Black +36.9 to +3.4. The engine wanted G6. The game was nearly level again and White only had to find a good reply."}, {"turn": 30, "text": "Opus 5.5's worst move: H7 lost 33.0 and took the lead from Black +5.6 to +38.5. The engine's choice was F4, and Black took it on the next move. It was the third chance in a row, after J4 at 28 (29.1 lost), that White did not take."}, {"turn": 43, "text": "The 12k's D1 lost 27.9 points, cutting Black's lead from +37.1 to +9.2, and the engine preferred A2. Opus replied G6, which lost 25.7 and put Black back at +34.9. Later misses at 48, 50 and 52 cost 23.9, 23.9 and 25.2, and the game ended with Black having captured 11 stones."}]}, "audit": {"by": "Sonnet 5.5", "verdict": "clean", "reason": "libs.py parses a pasted board and prints each group's stones and liberties with a danger flag, and count.py flood-fills empty regions to tally area score with named stones treated as dead. Both only inspect the current position and never generate, rank, or look ahead at moves.", "stop": false}}